@rekram1-node i gave this a go, and tested it for the day.

Did a red / green approach, see the commits here: https://github.com/rwese/opencode/commits/pr-4799/

If you have any further hints or requests, I can take a stab at it.

I use this plugin and the session idle definitely fires for me:
```
import type { Plugin } from "@opencode-ai/plugin";

export const Notify: Plugin = async ({ client, $ }) => {
  return {
    async event({ event }) {
      switch (event.type) {
        case "session.idle":
          await client.tui.showToast({
            body: {
              title: "[debug] event",
              message: event.type,
              variant: "info",
            },
          });
          break;
      }
    },
  };
};
```
